    9608/    F198 :                     		; We now perform the y portion of a bounding box check.  To do this, we assume a
    9609/    F198 :                     		; coordinate system where the y origin is at the highest y position relative to the object
    9610/    F198 :                     		; at which Sonic would still collide with it.  This point is
    9611/    F198 :                     		;   y_pos(object) - width(object)/2 - y_radius(Sonic) - 4,
    9612/    F198 :                     		; where object is stored in (a0), Sonic in (a1), and height(object)/2 in d2.  This way
    9613/    F198 :                     		; of doing it causes the object's hitbox to be vertically off-center by -4 pixels.
    9614/    F198 : 1629 0016           		move.b	obHeight(a1),d3			; load Sonic's y radius
    9615/    F19C : 4883                		ext.w	d3
